      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: redact diagnostic config fields with schema hints [AI]",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users exporting Gateway diagnostics could receive a support bundle whose sanitized config missed schema-marked sensitive provider request fields when those fields had generic names.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe diagnostics export now runs config sanitization through the same schema hint redaction path used by config-facing surfaces before applying support-bundle redaction. Support output also converts the internal redaction sentinel to the public `<redacted>` marker so exported JSON remains readable and contains no internal marker values.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can share diagnostics bundles with fewer manual checks around provider request auth and TLS transport settings. Existing shape summaries, log redaction, status snapshots, and health snapshots are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- AI-assisted.\n- `corepack pnpm exec oxfmt --write --threads=1 src/logging/diagnostic-support-export.ts src/logging/diagnostic-support-redaction.ts src/logging/diagnostic-support-export.test.ts`\n- AWS Crabbox focused test passed: `corepack pnpm test src/logging/diagnostic-support-export.test.ts` on `run_cecb06fbaf6c`, lease `cbx_96242da8d98d`, 10 tests passed.\n",
